<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌣 LIVE UV INDEX</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE UV INDEX</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> valid 2026-09-24 05:00 PM EDT (run 2026-09-24 08:00 AM EDT, forecast hour +9)<br/><b>Source updated:</b> Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:26:22 GMT<br/><b>Source version:</b> uvi-20260924-t12z-f09<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-24 05:24 PM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT FORECAST (12Z run)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/uv_index/legend.png?v=uvi-20260924-t12z-f09" width="600" alt="legend"><br>UV Index (UV Index), fixed absolute scale: <b>LOWEST 0</b> (green, low) → 3-5 (yellow, moderate) → 6-7 (orange, high) → 8-10 (red, very high) → <b>HIGHEST+ 11+</b> (violet, extreme). Same index always shows the same color. Current maximum over the lakes: <b>2.6</b>.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP CPC Global UV Index, operational GRIB2 (12 UTC GFS run, hourly steps to 120 h)<br/><a href="https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/stratosphere/uv_index/uv_global.shtml">https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/stratosphere/uv_index/uv_global.shtml</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE UV INDEX</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE UV INDEX</h2><p>Erythemal (sunburning) UV Index at the lake surface from the newest 12 UTC NCEP run, forecast hour nearest the current time. A forecast field, not a satellite observation: the displayed hour advances as time passes.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/uv_index/legend.png?v=uvi-20260924-t12z-f09" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>UV Index (UV Index), fixed absolute scale: <b>LOWEST 0</b> (green, low) → 3-5 (yellow, moderate) → 6-7 (orange, high) → 8-10 (red, very high) → <b>HIGHEST+ 11+</b> (violet, extreme). Same index always shows the same color. Current maximum over the lakes: <b>2.6</b>.</p><p><b>Units:</b> UV Index<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP CPC Global UV Index, operational GRIB2 (12 UTC GFS run, hourly steps to 120 h)<br/><b>Source run:</b> 2026-09-24 08:00 AM EDT<br/><b>Forecast hour:</b> +9h<br/><b>Valid time:</b> 2026-09-24 05:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> uvi-20260924-t12z-f09<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-24 05:24 PM EDT<br/><b>Why high values turn red/purple:</b> Extreme UV (11+) compresses into violet/deep-purple; ordinary low/moderate values own most of the color resolution.<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/stratosphere/uv_index/uv_global.shtml">CPC UV documentation</a></p>]]></description>
      <GroundOverlay>
